    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe endpoint now records, at create time, how many existing owners already shared the new owner's `firstName` + `lastName` (case-insensitively), and returns it as `namesakeCount` on the owner. Six files, each touched minimally:\n\n1. **`AssignNamesakeCount.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained function class (`WMC_other = 0`) that counts pre-existing namesakes via `ownerRepository.findAll()` before the new owner is saved, then calls `owner.setNamesakeCount(count)`.\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted one `assignNamesakeCount` step between `assignHousehold` and `save`, so the count is taken while the new owner is not yet persisted (`findAll()` sees only prior owners, matching the \"before this create\" semantics \u2014 same timing the existing `AssignCustomerCode` relies on).\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `namesake_count` column field plus a plain getter/setter (CC 1 each), following the existing `customerCode`/`householdId` pattern.\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` property to the `Owner` schema; MapStruct maps it name-for-name into the DTO automatically, so no mapper edit was needed.\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** / **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the nullable column and appended the matching value to the ten positional seed inserts (hsqldb is the test profile with `ddl-auto=none`).\n\nI left the h2/mysql/postgres seed data alone: h2 (the default run profile) uses column-list inserts and `ddl-auto=update`, so it picks up the new column without edits.\n\nThe provided test `coreCountsNamesakes` creates two owners named \"Ann Sur\u2026\" and asserts the second's `GET` returns `namesakeCount = 1` \u2014 it passes, and it's the only test in the suite.",
